# UI mount — do not apply while #328 (Scene3DWorkspace) or unified-layout (App/MainContent) owns those files.
# After those PRs land, one of the following is enough.

## Preferred: Video 3D workspace (has document + workspace)

In `ui/src/features/scene3d/Scene3DWorkspace.tsx`:

```tsx
import { ProjectTransferDialog } from '../project-transfer'
```

Near `Scene3DDocumentControls`:

```tsx
const [transferOpen, setTransferOpen] = useState(false)
```

```tsx
<button type="button" className="min-h-10 rounded-lg border border-border px-3" disabled={editingLocked}
  onClick={() => setTransferOpen(true)}>Transfer project</button>
<ProjectTransferDialog
  open={transferOpen}
  onClose={() => setTransferOpen(false)}
  workspace={workspace}
  documents={[sceneDoc]}
  onImported={() => { /* optional: reopen library */ }}
/>
```

## Alternative: editor chrome (not App/MainContent)

`ui/src/features/scene3d/Scene3DEditorPanel.tsx` can host the same dialog if it receives `workspace` and `documents` from a parent. Do not reach into `useStore` from this package.

## Optional i18n catalog (dialog already ships EN/ES)

Only if an integrator wants the strings in `resources.ts`. Copy:

- `ui/src/features/project-transfer/locales/en.json` → `ui/src/i18n/locales/en/projectTransfer.json`
- `ui/src/features/project-transfer/locales/es.json` → `ui/src/i18n/locales/es/projectTransfer.json`

Then in `ui/src/i18n/resources.ts` add `projectTransfer` to `NAMESPACES` and both `resources.en` / `resources.es`. Also add the name to `ui/scripts/check-i18n-catalogs.mjs` `NAMESPACES`.
